## Source
Path B UX dry-run (0152), severity: **High**

## Context
README step 2 says "the committed `tickets/erg` in this repo is the prebuilt
binary: copy it, no download needed." This is only true if the user is inside
a clone of git-erg. For the primary use case — installing into a new project —
there is no binary to copy. The agent improvised a `curl` of the raw GitHub URL;
this is undocumented and breaks for private forks, tagged releases, or users
who distrust raw CDN downloads.

## Fix
Add a one-line download command immediately after "copy it, no download needed",
for users not inside a git-erg clone. Something like:

```bash
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg/main/tickets/erg \
  -o tickets/erg && chmod +x tickets/erg
```

Or a `gh release download` variant once releases are tagged.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] README "Install into a project" step 2 includes a concrete download command
- [ ] The command works from a clean directory with no git-erg clone present
